uestion/answer-fields "answer-field-1632bbd1-d312-5a7f-a64f-22e3b1a7ff52"] ["question-cfa20750-c86e-5358-ae72-96466e6a1578" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-833c84b1-7ee9-574b-9a22-60778f19bb83"] ["question-cfa20750-c86e-5358-ae72-96466e6a1578" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-f111d030-ce88-5d03-9b99-a627f5567a44"] ["question-cfa20750-c86e-5358-ae72-96466e6a1578" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-17626623-6533-5b07-939c-3abf99298482"] [17592186204098 :knowledge-point/questions "question-cfa20750-c86e-5358-ae72-96466e6a1578"] [17592186204588 :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))\n$$\n\nis the product of a$\\,\\,${{field-1}}$\\times ${{field-2}} \nmatrix with a \n{{field-3}} $\\times $ {{field-4}} \nmatrix, which results in a \n{{field-5}} $\\times $ {{field-6}} \nmatrix."] [17592186204588 :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the product\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nof a $3\\times 2$ matrix with a $2\\times 2$ matrix is a $3\\times 2$ matrix."] [17592186204588 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-cb36d833-b