203449 :answer-field/choices "answer-0fa2bc32-5eea-5d94-9810-072ac4a32c58"] ["answer-65c8f86c-8629-5c20-b24f-d9af3606d2ec" :answer/id #uuid "65c8f86c-8629-5c20-b24f-d9af3606d2ec"] ["answer-65c8f86c-8629-5c20-b24f-d9af3606d2ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-65c8f86c-8629-5c20-b24f-d9af3606d2ec" :answer/value "2"] [17592186203450 :answer-field/correct "answer-65c8f86c-8629-5c20-b24f-d9af3606d2ec"] [17592186203450 :answer-field/choices "answer-65c8f86c-8629-5c20-b24f-d9af3606d2ec"] ["question-5b9f6727-3d7f-553c-90bd-4d6b87d491ad" :question/id #uuid "5b9f6727-3d7f-553c-90bd-4d6b87d491ad"] ["question-5b9f6727-3d7f-553c-90bd-4d6b87d491ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-269762"] ["question-5b9f6727-3d7f-553c-90bd-4d6b87d491ad" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{4}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}6{y}_{1}+1 \\\\ {y}_{1}{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nAccording to the chain rule, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))\n$$\n\nis the product of a$\\,\\,${{field-1}}$\\times ${{field-2}} \nmatrix with a \n{{field-3}} $\\times $ {{field-4}} \nmatrix, which results in a \n{{field-5}} $\\times $ {{field-6}} \nmatrix."] ["question-5b9f6727-3d7f-553c-90bd-4d6b87d491ad" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{4}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, the product\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\n$$\n\nof a $2\\times 2$ matrix with a $2\\times 4$ matrix is a $2\\times 4$ matrix."] ["question-5b9f6727-3d7f-553c-90bd-4d6b87d491ad" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-97c12cb8-5725-50f2-aa29-32cc8b67a848" :answer-field/id #uuid "97c12cb8-5725-50f2-aa29-32cc8b67a848"] ["answer-f8b053af-73e3-5382-bd96-6c77018b08b6" :answer/id #uuid "f8b053af-73e3-5382-bd96-6c77018b08b6"] ["answer-f8b053af-73e3-5382-bd96-6c77018b08b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f8b053af-73e3-5382-bd96-6c77018b08b6" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-97c12cb8-5725-50f2-aa29-32cc8b67a848" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-97c12cb8-5725-50f2-aa29-32cc8b67a848" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-97c12cb8-5725-50f2-aa29-32cc8b67a848" :answer-field/correct "answer-f8b053af-73e3-5382-bd96-6c77018b08b6"] ["answer-field-97c12cb8-5725-50f2-aa29-32cc8b67a848" :answer-field/choices "answer-f8b053af-73e3-5382-bd96-6c77018b08b6"] ["answer-field-f3e88de5-3537-5d05-b414-2095d1fba253" :answer-field/id #uuid "f3e88de5-3537-5d05-b414-2095d1fba253"] ["answer-b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94" :answer/id #uuid "b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94"] ["answer-b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-f3e88de5-3537-5d05-b414-2095d1fba253" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-f3e88de5-3537-5d05-b414-2095d1fba253" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-f3e88de5-3537-5d05-b414-2095d1fba253" :answer-field/correct "answer-b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94"] ["answer-field-f3e88de5-3537-5d05-b414-2095d1fba253" :answer-field/choices "answer-b820369c-81ff-58ee-a127-e2d6233a0b94"] ["answer-field-a058cc13-5200-5985-ace8-aa6e1663852a" :answer-field/id #uuid "a058cc13-5200-5985-ace8-aa6e1663852a"] ["answer-2f29be1f-cf21-5f6b-9fdd-561e8c1eb42f" :answer/id #uuid "2f29be1f-cf