-d5f13bdb4255"] ["question-316244d1-8305-5968-b730-d6310a788240" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-14e2587d-142c-5f42-b805-a2dc168df701"] ["question-316244d1-8305-5968-b730-d6310a788240" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-288a36d8-5d2d-567a-9ad2-820a7533c15d"] [17592186204099 :knowledge-point/questions "question-316244d1-8305-5968-b730-d6310a788240"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/id #uuid "fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/math-academy-id "q-270269"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ and $f:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2},$ defined by\n\n$$\ny(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,f(y)=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}{y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is \n$\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at \n${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $f$ with respect to $y$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{y}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{y}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}(2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}(2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{1}}({y}_{1}^{3}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{y}_{2}}({y}_{1}^{3})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{2} & 2{y}_{1} \\\\ 3{y}_{1}^{2} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${y}_{0}=y({x}_{0})=[\\begin{aligned}2(1) \\\\ 3(-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus, the total derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{y}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(2{x}_{1}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(2{x}_{1}) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(3{x}_{2}^{2}) & \\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(3{x}_{2}^{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at ${x}_{0}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)){|}_{{x}_{0}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}{|}_{{y}_{0}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{{x}_{0}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & -24 \\\\ 24 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd"] ["answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer/id #uuid "5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6"] ["answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6" :answer/value "12"] ["answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/correct "answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6"] ["answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd" :answer-field/choices "answer-5357d450-abcf-50c3-96bd-a1511a8aa0b6"] ["answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398"] ["answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer/id #uuid "321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1"] ["answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1" :answer/value "-24"] ["answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/correct "answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1"] ["answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398" :answer-field/choices "answer-321d5e82-c48e-5811-888e-74d3e2581bb1"] ["answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/id #uuid "df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170"] ["answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer/id #uuid "709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347"] ["answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347" :answer/value "24"] ["answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/key "field-3"] ["answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/correct "answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347"] ["answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170" :answer-field/choices "answer-709cce09-0567-5921-b471-91435e0f6347"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0ca9696c-ed27-5b5d-bd05-4135421712bd"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-d9519eb4-2f77-527e-8bce-eeaa7fb7a398"] ["question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-df962cc0-8c0f-5244-9b84-5776766a0170"] [17592186204099 :knowledge-point/questions "question-fdb98924-99f5-55a4-8e7e-a090dae96539"] ["question-a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/id #uuid "a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1"] ["question-a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-269812"] ["question-a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/problem "Consider the functions $y(x)=Ax$ and $f(y)=By,$ where $x\\in {R}^{2},y\\in {R}^{3},$ and the matrices $A$ and $B$ are given by\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))$ evaluated at ${x}_{0}=[3,\\,-2]^{T}?$\n\n<table cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"70px\" rowspan=\"2\" width=\"30px\">\n${\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))|}_{{x}_{0}}=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">$7$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] ["question-a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/worked-solution "Using the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x))=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet's consider each of the factors in turn.\n\n- The function $f$ acts on a vector $y\\in {R}^{3}$ by multiplying it by $B$ and outputs a vector $f(y)\\in {R}^{2}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}=B.\n$$\n\n- The function $y$ acts on a vector $x\\in {R}^{2}$ by multiplying it by $A$ and outputs a vector $y(x)\\in {R}^{3}.$ Thus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}f(y(x)) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =BA \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 23 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-a62becc2-1daf-5292-96cb-be1f422032a1" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c"] ["answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer/id #uuid "9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875"] ["answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-field-6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/correct "answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875"] ["answer-field-6d1e6843-8b9f-57b5-9c3f-415b575af25c" :answer-field/choices "answer-9bff7b7c-75ce-5613-b082-0122e4795875"] ["answer-field-763c8765-